{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ2p39LoRMt8zotQQdST","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't get the bps figure. The guidance range and the exact actual margin weren't readable with these tools.\n\n**Answer: TJX appears to have beaten its Q4 FY2025 pre-tax margin guidance, but I couldn't confirm by how many bps.**\n\n- **What the search found:** The search tool shows matching filings but not their text. TJX's Q4 FY2025 earnings release (8-K, filed 26 Feb 2025) contains both \"pretax profit margin of 11.6%\" and \"above the high end\". That suggests a Q4 pre-tax margin of about 11.6%, above the top of plan. Because I can't see the text, I can't confirm that the 11.6% is the Q4 figure rather than another period or a non-GAAP measure.\n- **What's missing:** The guidance was in the Q3 FY2025 earnings release (8-K, filed 20 Nov 2024). I couldn't get the actual range from it. Exact-phrase searches for \"11.0% to 11.1%\", \"11.1% to 11.2%\" and \"11.3% to 11.4%\" found nothing. I reached the tool-call budget before trying other wordings.\n\nTo get the bps beat, take the high end of the Q4 range from the 20 Nov 2024 release and subtract it from the actual Q4 margin in the 26 Feb 2025 release. Each 0.1 percentage point equals 10 bps.\n\n**Sources**\n- TJX 8-K (Q4 FY2025 earnings release), filed 2025-02-26, accession 0000109198-25-000006\n- TJX 8-K (Q3 FY2025 earnings release, which has the Q4 guidance), filed 2024-11-20, accession 0000109198-24-000056"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":8865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i